  "ai_language_tip": "English (en) works for almost all business calls; Afrikaans (af) is common in the Western/Northern Cape and farm towns, isiZulu (zu) and other African languages in many areas — reply in them only if the other side switches.",
  "english_ok": "yes — English is the main business language nationwide; accents vary, and some rural staff prefer Afrikaans or an African language.",
  "politeness": "Friendly and informal-polite; open with 'Good morning/afternoon, how are you?' and hear the reply before business — skipping the greeting feels rude; 'Sir/Ma'am' common; close with 'Thank you, have a good day'.",
  "name_tip": "Bookings under surname or first name; Afrikaans surnames with prefixes (van der, du, de) and Nguni names may need spelling; use the NATO alphabet for spelling.",
  "phone_tip": "All numbers 10 digits with 0: mobile 06/07/08 (e.g. 082 12345678), Johannesburg 011, Cape Town 021; international +27; WhatsApp is the default for confirmations.",
  "time_tip": "24h in writing ('19:30'); speech mostly 12h with am/pm. Afrikaans 'halfagt' = 7:30 (half to eight)! Treat 'just now' as vague; always confirm an exact clock time.",
  "number_tip": "Numbers read digit by digit in groups 3-3-4; 'double' and 'triple' common ('double five'); beware 'now now' (soon) and 'just now' (later, could be hours) for time promises.",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid calls after 19:00 for trades and offices, restaurant peaks 12:30–14:00 and 18:30–20:30, Sunday for offices, and the December–early January holiday shutdown.",
  "closed_days": "Shops and malls open daily; many offices and practices close weekends or Saturday afternoon; holidays include 1 January, 21 March, Good Friday, Family Day (Easter Monday), 27 April, 1 May, 16 June, 9 August, 24 September, 16, 25 and 26 December; a holiday on Sunday moves to Monday.",
  "booking_channels": "Dineplan and venue websites for restaurants; phone and WhatsApp very common for doctors, salons and trades; practice booking pages; Mr D and Uber Eats for delivery; Uber and Bolt for rides.",
  "voice_menu": "Medical aids, banks, Vodacom/MTN/Cell C/Telkom, municipalities and couriers use IVR; GP and dentist receptionists answer directly.",
  "callback_habits": "Dineplan and practices send SMS/e-mail confirmations; small businesses confirm by WhatsApp; restaurants may call to confirm large bookings.",
